{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 80,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim Eduth, A Psalm of Asaph. Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel, thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "between",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the cherubim, shine forth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh stir up thy strength, and come ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " save us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn us again, O God, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy people?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou feedest them with the bread of tears; and givest them tears to drink in great measure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us a strife to our neighbors: and our enemies laugh among themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn us again, O God of hosts, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast brought a vine out of Egypt: thou hast cast out the heathen, and planted it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou preparedst ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "room",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before it, and didst cause it to take deep root, and it filled the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The hills were covered with the shade of it, and its boughs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the goodly cedars.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She sent out her boughs to the sea, and her branches to the river.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why hast thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " broke down her hedges, so that all they who pass by the way do pluck her?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The boar from the wood doth waste it, and the wild beast of the field doth devour it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the vineyard which thy right hand planted, and the branch ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou madest strong for thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " burnt with fire, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou madest strong for thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So will we not go back from thee: revive us, and we will call upon thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.80.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.80.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts, cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
